{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q5103099","formula":"C₂H₂Cl₂O₂","hill":"C2H2Cl2O2","elements":["H","C","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":2.0,"H":2.0,"O":2.0,"Cl":2.0},"names":{"en":"Chloromethyl chloroformate"},"descriptions":{"en":"Chloromethyl chloroformate (CClO2CH2Cl), also known as palite gas, is a chemical compound and used for chemical warfare during World War I. German forces used a mixture of chloromethyl chloroformate and dichloromethyl chloroformate called \"K-Stoff\", while French and other Allied forces used it under name \"Palite\". It is a tearing agent designed to cause temporary blindness. It is a colorless liquid with a penetrating, irritating odor."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":62754,"mass":128.94,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(OC(=O)Cl)Cl","inchikey":"JYWJULGYGOLCGW-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"chloromethyl carbonochloridate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"62754","atoms":8,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.862,"y":0.438,"z":-0.014,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-2.265,"y":1.075,"z":-0.004,"el":"Cl"},{"x":0.251,"y":0.434,"z":0.012,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.196,"y":-1.337,"z":-0.009,"el":"O"},{"x":1.349,"y":-0.484,"z":0.015,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.001,"y":-0.126,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.319,"y":-1.118,"z":-0.877,"el":"H"},{"x":1.335,"y":-1.09,"z":0.925,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,4,1],[1,5,1],[2,4,1],[2,5,1],[3,5,2],[4,6,1],[4,7,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5103099","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chloromethyl_chloroformate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"properties","name":"PubChem","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/62754","license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},{"role":"structure","name":"PubChem 3D","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov